From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 23:21:23 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mq-phanbell: Give the GPU power domain its
 supply

BUCK3 feeds the GPU rail but no consumer references it, and unlike every
other regulator on this board it is not marked regulator-always-on. Once
a driver for the BD71837 is present the regulator core therefore finds
it unused and turns it off when it completes initialisation:

  buck3: disabling

which kills the board about thirty seconds into the boot.

Describe the actual relationship instead of pinning the rail on: hand
BUCK3 to the GPU power domain, the same way imx8mq-librem5.dtsi does.
The domain then holds the reference while the GPU is powered and the
core no longer considers the regulator unused.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
index e34045d..f8bd1e4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
@@ -259,6 +259,10 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&pgc_gpu {
+	power-supply = <&buck3>;
+};
+
 &fec1 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_fec1>;
